('fixed:gh-4154', 'fixed', '{"id": "gh-4154", "number": 4154, "title": "openai-responses strips prompt_cache_breakpoint content-block metadata (GPT-5.6 prefix caching doesn''t work)", "repros": [{"files": {"baml_src/test.baml": "function EditSentence(stable: string, suffix: string) -> string {\n  client LunaResponses\n  prompt #\"\n    {{ _.role(\"system\") }}\n    You are a copy editor. Reply with the edited sentence only.\n\n    {{ _.role(\"user\", prompt_cache_breakpoint={\"mode\": \"explicit\"}) }}\n    {{ stable }}\n\n    {{ _.role(\"user\") }}\n    Now edit this sentence: {{ suffix }}\n  \"#\n}\n", "baml_src/clients.baml": "client<llm> LunaResponses {\n  provider openai-responses\n  retry_policy Constant\n  options {\n    model \"gpt-5.6-luna\"\n    api_key env.OPENAI_API_KEY\n    reasoning { effort \"low\" }\n    allowed_role_metadata [\"prompt_cache_breakpoint\"]\n  }\n}\n\nretry_policy Constant {\n  max_retries 1\n}\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "baml-cli dev --request-only EditSentence", "expectation": {"check": "requires_inspection", "instructions": "Inspect the HTTP request body the openai-responses provider builds for EditSentence. The `input_text` content block carrying `stable` must include the `prompt_cache_breakpoint` field with value `{\"mode\": \"explicit\"}`. Currently the field is absent from the serialized content block. No live API call is required to observe the defect."}}, {"files": {"baml_src/test.baml": "function EditSentence(stable: string, suffix: string) -> string {\n  client LunaResponses\n  prompt #\"\n    {{ _.role(\"system\") }}\n    You are a copy editor. Reply with the edited sentence only.\n\n    {{ _.role(\"user\", prompt_cache_breakpoint={\"mode\": \"explicit\"}) }}\n    {{ stable }}\n\n    {{ _.role(\"user\") }}\n    Now edit this sentence: {{ suffix }}\n  \"#\n}\n", "baml_src/clients.baml": "client<llm> LunaResponses {\n  provider openai-responses\n  retry_policy Constant\n  options {\n    model \"gpt-5.6-luna\"\n    api_key env.OPENAI_API_KEY\n    reasoning { effort \"low\" }\n    allowed_role_metadata [\"prompt_cache_breakpoint\"]\n  }\n}\n\nretry_policy Constant {\n  max_retries 1\n}\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "baml-cli test", "expectation": {"check": "requires_inspection", "instructions": "Live end-to-end check against OpenAI. Call EditSentence 4 times with an identical ~4,000-token `stable` argument and a different `suffix` each iteration, reading `cachedInputTokens` from a collector. Iteration 0 is a cold cache write; iterations 1-3 should report a high cached-token ratio (the direct Responses API with the breakpoint forwarded returns ~99%). Today iterations 1-3 report 0%. Control arm: repeat with a byte-identical full prompt every iteration and no breakpoint metadata - that arm already reports ~100% cached on iterations 1-3, so a failure there indicates an unrelated environment problem rather than this defect."}}], "closed_on_github": true}'::jsonb, 'eval'),
('fixed:gh-4279', 'fixed', '{"id": "gh-4279", "number": 4279, "title": "[bug]  `baml pack --target *-unknown-linux-musl` always fails: \"Unsupported sh_offset value 0x238 for section ''.hash''\"", "repros": [{"files": {"t.baml": "function main() -> string {\n    \"tiny ok\"\n}\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "baml pack main --file t.baml --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl -o out-musl", "expectation": {"check": "should_compile"}}, {"files": {"t.baml": "function main() -> string {\n    \"tiny ok\"\n}\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "baml pack main --file t.baml --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu -o out-gnu", "expectation": {"check": "should_compile"}}, {"files": {"t.baml": "function main() -> string {\n    \"tiny ok\"\n}\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "baml pack main --file t.baml --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl -o out-musl; ls -l out-musl", "expectation": {"check": "requires_inspection", "instructions": "Secondary defect: a failing musl pack must not leave an artifact at the -o path. Currently a 0-byte `out-musl` remains, which build scripts mistake for a successful artifact. Verify that after a failed pack the output file is absent, or (once the primary fix lands) that the pack succeeds and out-musl is a non-empty valid ELF. To confirm the underlying cause on the shipped musl pack host: `readelf -lW bin/baml-pack-host | grep -c NOTE` => 0; phdr start/size/count => 64/56/9 (table ends at 0x238); `readelf -SW bin/baml-pack-host | grep ''\\.hash''` => .hash starts at 0x238, zero slack."}}], "closed_on_github": true}'::jsonb, 'eval'),
('fixed:gh-4335', 'fixed', '{"id": "gh-4335", "number": 4335, "title": "rust codegen panics on `naming_convention = \"language\"` instead of emitting a diagnostic", "repros": [{"files": {"baml.toml": "[package]\nname = \"bamltest\"\n\n[generator.rust_client]\noutput_type = \"rust\"\noutput_dir = \"./baml_rust\"\nnaming_convention = \"language\"\n", "baml_src/main.baml": "function main() -> string {\n  \"hello from baml\"\n}\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "baml-cli generate", "expectation": {"check": "requires_inspection", "instructions": "`baml-cli generate` must not panic. It should exit nonzero and print a diagnostic naming the generator (`rust_client`) and stating that `naming_convention = \"language\"` is unsupported for `output_type = \"rust\"`, suggesting `\"preserve-case\"`. Failure: stderr contains `panicked at` or `only NamingConvention::PreserveCase is supported`."}}, {"files": {"baml.toml": "[package]\nname = \"bamltest\"\n\n[generator.rust_client]\noutput_type = \"rust\"\noutput_dir = \"./baml_rust\"\nnaming_convention = \"preserve-case\"\n", "baml_src/main.baml": "function main() -> string {\n  \"hello from baml\"\n}\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "baml-cli generate", "expectation": {"check": "requires_inspection", "instructions": "Control case, reported working today and must stay working: generation succeeds, exits zero, and emits Rust client sources under ./baml_rust."}}], "closed_on_github": true}'::jsonb, 'eval'),
('fixed:gh-4355', 'fixed', '{"id": "gh-4355", "number": 4355, "title": "[bug] @boundaryml/baml-bridge-linux-x64-musl ships a glibc binary — addon fails to load on Alpine", "repros": [{"files": {"Dockerfile": "FROM node:22-alpine\nRUN npm install @boundaryml/baml-bridge@0.15.0\nRUN node -e \"require(''@boundaryml/baml-bridge'')\"\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "docker build .", "expectation": {"check": "requires_inspection", "instructions": "The build must succeed: `require(''@boundaryml/baml-bridge'')` loads the native addon on a stock node:22-alpine image with no gcompat or other glibc shim installed. Currently the build fails with napi''s fallback message \"Cannot find native binding. npm has a bug related to optional dependencies ...\". Requiring the addon directly (`node -e \"require(''/app/node_modules/@boundaryml/baml-bridge-linux-x64-musl/baml_node.linux-x64-musl.node'')\"`) shows the underlying error: \"Error loading shared library ld-linux-x86-64.so.2: No such file or directory\"."}}, {"files": {"check-musl-artifact.sh": "#!/bin/sh\nset -e\nnpm pack @boundaryml/baml-bridge-linux-x64-musl@0.15.0\ntar -xzf boundaryml-baml-bridge-linux-x64-musl-0.15.0.tgz\n\necho ''--- NEEDED ---''\nreadelf -d package/baml_node.linux-x64-musl.node | grep NEEDED\n\necho ''--- GLIBC versioned symbols ---''\nreadelf -V package/baml_node.linux-x64-musl.node | grep -oE ''GLIBC_[0-9.]+'' | sort -uV | tail -3\n\n# release gate\nif readelf -V package/baml_node.linux-x64-musl.node | grep -q ''GLIBC_''; then\n  echo ''musl artifact is glibc-linked''\n  exit 1\nfi\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "sh check-musl-artifact.sh", "expectation": {"check": "requires_inspection", "instructions": "Platform-independent; no Alpine host needed. The script must exit 0: the NEEDED list should contain libc.musl-x86-64.so.1 and no libc.so.6 / ld-linux-x86-64.so.2, and no GLIBC_* versioned symbols should be present. Currently NEEDED lists libgcc_s.so.1, libc.so.6, ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 and versioned symbols go up to GLIBC_2.34, so the gate exits 1 with ''musl artifact is glibc-linked''."}}, {"files": {"compare-artifacts.sh": "#!/bin/sh\nset -e\nnpm pack @boundaryml/baml-bridge-linux-x64-musl@0.15.1-nightly.20260809.a\ntar -xzf boundaryml-baml-bridge-linux-x64-musl-0.15.1-nightly.20260809.a.tgz\nreadelf -d package/baml_node.linux-x64-musl.node | grep NEEDED\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "sh compare-artifacts.sh", "expectation": {"check": "requires_inspection", "instructions": "Confirms there is no fixed version to upgrade to. The newest published nightly must link libc.musl-x86-64.so.1; currently it reports the identical glibc NEEDED set (libgcc_s.so.1, libc.so.6, ld-linux-x86-64.so.2) as 0.15.0."}}], "closed_on_github": true}'::jsonb, 'eval'),
('fixed:gh-4370', 'fixed', '{"id": "gh-4370", "number": 4370, "title": "sdkgen_rust 0.16: every LLM function is skipped (implicit ai.errors.Failure throws contract is an interface) — empty client at exit 0", "repros": [{"files": {"baml.toml": "[package]\nname = \"probe\"\n\n[generator.rust_client]\noutput_type = \"rust\"\nnaming_convention = \"preserve-case\"\noutput_dir = \"crates\"\n", "baml_src/main.baml": "client Probe = openai.OpenAiClient.new(model = \"gpt-4o-mini\");\n\nclass Thing {\n  name string\n}\n\nfunction ProbeFn(text: string) -> Thing {\n  client Probe\n  prompt `Extract a thing from: ${text}\n\n${ctx.output_format}`\n}\n"}, "setup": "export BAML_VERSION=0.16.0", "command": "baml generate", "expectation": {"check": "requires_inspection", "instructions": "Generation must not silently succeed with zero emitted functions. Either `baml generate` emits ProbeFn into a generated Rust crate under crates/ with a representable error type for the implicit ai.errors.Failure throws contract, or it exits non-zero. FAIL if the command exits 0 while ProbeFn is absent from the output. Currently: exits 0, no crates/ output, stderr has `warning: skipped user.ProbeFn: throws contract: unsupported union arm: ai.errors.Failure`."}}, {"files": {"baml.toml": "[package]\nname = \"probe\"\n\n[generator.rust_client]\noutput_type = \"rust\"\nnaming_convention = \"preserve-case\"\noutput_dir = \"crates\"\n", "baml_src/main.baml": "client Probe = openai.OpenAiClient.new(model = \"gpt-4o-mini\");\n\nclass Thing {\n  name string\n}\n\nfunction ProbeFn(text: string) -> Thing {\n  client Probe\n  prompt `Extract a thing from: ${text}\n\n${ctx.output_format}`\n}\n"}, "setup": "export BAML_VERSION=0.16.0", "command": "baml generate -F beta && grep -c ProbeFn crates/*/src/lib.rs", "expectation": {"check": "requires_inspection", "instructions": "Under the beta generator path the written lib.rs must contain ProbeFn. FAIL if `baml generate -F beta` exits 0 and the grep count for ProbeFn is 0. Currently: exit 0, lib.rs written, grep -c ProbeFn returns 0 — an empty client rather than a missing one."}}, {"files": {"baml.toml": "[package]\nname = \"probe\"\n\n[generator.rust_client]\noutput_type = \"rust\"\nnaming_convention = \"preserve-case\"\noutput_dir = \"crates\"\n", "baml_src/main.baml": "client Probe = openai.OpenAiClient.new(model = \"gpt-4o-mini\");\n\nclass Thing {\n  name string\n}\n\nfunction ProbeFn(text: string) -> Thing throws ai.errors.RateLimited | ai.errors.NetworkFailure\n  | ai.errors.InvalidRequest | ai.errors.Refused | ai.errors.ParseFailed\n  | ai.errors.StepBudgetExceeded | ai.errors.ToolFailedError | ai.errors.StreamingUnsupported\n  | baml.errors.InvalidArgument | baml.errors.UnknownError {\n  client Probe\n  prompt `Extract a thing from: ${text}\n\n${ctx.output_format}`\n}\n"}, "setup": "export BAML_VERSION=0.16.0", "command": "baml generate", "expectation": {"check": "should_compile"}}], "closed_on_github": true}'::jsonb, 'eval'),
('fixed:gh-4421', 'fixed', '{"id": "gh-4421", "number": 4421, "title": "[bug] for loop with multi-variable reassignment + array push hangs (0.15.0) / throws spurious VM type error (0.16.0)", "repros": [{"files": {"baml_src/repro.baml": "class Fact {\n    subject_id: string,\n    section: string,\n    text: string,\n}\n\nfunction parse_subject_file(content: string, subject_id: string) -> Fact[] {\n    let facts: Fact[] = [];\n    let current_section = \"\";\n    let in_scope = false;\n    for (let raw_line in content.lines()) {\n        let line = raw_line.trim();\n        if (line.starts_with(\"## \")) {\n            let heading = line.substring(3, line.length());\n            in_scope = heading != \"One-Sentence Takeaway\" && heading != \"References & Rabbit Holes\";\n            current_section = heading;\n        } else if (in_scope && line.starts_with(\"- \")) {\n            let _ = facts.push(Fact { subject_id: subject_id, section: current_section, text: line.substring(2, line.length()) });\n        }\n    }\n    facts\n}\n\ntest \"repro\" {\n    let content = #\"# Created Pipeline (Marketing)\n\n---\n\n## 1. First Idea\n\n- Bullet one here.\n\n## 2. Second Idea\n\n- Bullet two here.\n\"#;\n    let facts = parse_subject_file(content, \"x\");\n    assert.equal(facts.length(), 2)\n}\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "baml test", "expectation": {"check": "requires_inspection", "instructions": "The test must terminate and must not emit `VM internal error: type error: ...`. On canary 0.15.0 this command is expected to hang indefinitely (>600s); on canary 0.16.0 it is expected to fail fast with `VM internal error: type error: expected string, got bool` originating from run_test/test_child in <builtin>/testing/registry.baml. Correct behavior: the test passes (two facts parsed), or at worst reports a plain assertion failure. The reporter could not reproduce this in a fresh scaffolded project - if it passes as-is, pad baml_src/ with additional functions/files or reuse a warm .baml/profiles/ cache to increase enclosing program size before concluding it is fixed."}}, {"files": {"baml_src/repro.baml": "class Fact {\n    subject_id: string,\n    section: string,\n    text: string,\n}\n\nfunction parse_subject_file(content: string, subject_id: string) -> Fact[] {\n    let facts: Fact[] = [];\n    let current_section = \"\";\n    let in_scope = false;\n    for (let raw_line in content.lines()) {\n        let line = raw_line.trim();\n        if (line.starts_with(\"## \")) {\n            let heading = line.substring(3, line.length());\n            in_scope = heading != \"One-Sentence Takeaway\" && heading != \"References & Rabbit Holes\";\n            current_section = heading;\n        } else if (in_scope && line.starts_with(\"- \")) {\n            let _ = facts.push(Fact { subject_id: subject_id, section: current_section, text: line.substring(2, line.length()) });\n        }\n    }\n    facts\n}\n\nfunction repro_main() -> json {\n    let content = #\"# Created Pipeline (Marketing)\n\n---\n\n## 1. First Idea\n\n- Bullet one here.\n\n## 2. Second Idea\n\n- Bullet two here.\n\"#;\n    let facts = parse_subject_file(content, \"x\");\n    facts.length()\n}\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "baml eval repro_main", "expectation": {"check": "should_evaluate_to", "expected": 2}}, {"files": {"baml_src/repro.baml": "class Fact {\n    subject_id: string,\n    section: string,\n    text: string,\n}\n\nfunction parse_subject_file(content: string, subject_id: string) -> Fact[] {\n    let facts: Fact[] = [];\n    let current_section = \"\";\n    let in_scope = false;\n    for (let raw_line in content.lines()) {\n        let line = raw_line.trim();\n        if (line.starts_with(\"## \")) {\n            let heading = line.substring(3, line.length());\n            in_scope = heading != \"One-Sentence Takeaway\" && heading != \"References & Rabbit Holes\";\n            current_section = heading;\n        } else if (in_scope && line.starts_with(\"- \")) {\n            let _ = facts.push(Fact { subject_id: subject_id, section: current_section, text: line.substring(2, line.length()) });\n        }\n    }\n    facts\n}\n\n// Control: per the reporter''s bisection, dropping the bare `---` line and the\n// second heading/bullet pair makes the failure go away. This must keep passing.\nfunction repro_main() -> json {\n    let content = #\"# Created Pipeline (Marketing)\n\n## 1. First Idea\n\n- Bullet one here.\n\"#;\n    let facts = parse_subject_file(content, \"x\");\n    facts.length()\n}\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "baml eval repro_main", "expectation": {"check": "should_evaluate_to", "expected": 1}}], "closed_on_github": true}'::jsonb, 'eval'),
('fixed:gh-4468', 'fixed', '{"id": "gh-4468", "number": 4468, "title": "[bug] 0.17.0 canary: compiler ABORTS (SIGABRT) instead of reporting — `if`/`else` over an `Array.map` result, then iterated", "repros": [{"files": {"baml_src/repro.baml": "function repro(xs: int[], b: bool) -> int {\n    let ys = if (b) {\n        [0]\n    } else {\n        xs.map((x: int) -> int {\n            x + 1\n        })\n    };\n    let n = 0;\n    for (let y in ys) {\n        n = n + y;\n    }\n    n\n}\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "baml check", "expectation": {"check": "should_compile"}}, {"files": {"baml_src/repro.baml": "function repro(xs: int[], b: bool) -> int {\n    let ys: int[] = if (b) {\n        [0]\n    } else {\n        xs.map((x: int) -> int {\n            x + 1\n        })\n    };\n    let n = 0;\n    for (let y in ys) {\n        n = n + y;\n    }\n    n\n}\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "baml check", "expectation": {"check": "should_compile"}}, {"files": {"baml_src/repro.baml": "function repro_main() -> json {\n    let xs = [1, 2, 3];\n    let b = false;\n    let ys = if (b) {\n        [0]\n    } else {\n        xs.map((x: int) -> int {\n            x + 1\n        })\n    };\n    let n = 0;\n    for (let y in ys) {\n        n = n + y;\n    }\n    n\n}\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "baml run repro_main", "expectation": {"check": "should_evaluate_to", "expected": 9}}], "closed_on_github": true}'::jsonb, 'eval'),
('fixed:gh-4497', 'fixed', '{"id": "gh-4497", "number": 4497, "title": "[SEV-2 / BUG] BAML rejects valid Fireworks Chat Completions responses containing both completion_tokens_details and output_tokens_details", "repros": [{"files": {"test.ts": "import { b } from ''./baml_client''\nb.Extract(''hi'').then(console.log, (e) => console.error(String(e)))\n", "server.js": "const fs = require(''fs'')\nrequire(''http'').createServer((req, res) => res.end(fs.readFileSync(''response.json''))).listen(8787)\n", "response.json": "{\n  \"id\": \"chatcmpl-example\",\n  \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n  \"created\": 1787007845,\n  \"model\": \"accounts/fireworks/models/deepseek-v4-flash-0731\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    {\n      \"index\": 0,\n      \"message\": { \"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"synthetic summary text\", \"tools\": null },\n      \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"prompt_tokens\": 100,\n    \"completion_tokens\": 20,\n    \"total_tokens\": 120,\n    \"prompt_tokens_details\": { \"cached_tokens\": 99 },\n    \"completion_tokens_details\": { \"reasoning_tokens\": 0 },\n    \"output_tokens_details\": { \"reasoning_tokens\": 0 }\n  }\n}\n", "baml_src/main.baml": "generator ts {\n    output_type \"typescript\"\n    output_dir \"../\"\n    version \"0.225.0\"\n    default_client_mode async\n}\n\nclient<llm> Mock {\n    provider \"openai-generic\"\n    options {\n        base_url \"http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1\"\n        api_key \"x\"\n        model \"x\"\n    }\n}\n\nfunction Extract(text: string) -> string {\n    client Mock\n    prompt #\"{{ text }}\"#\n}\n"}, "setup": "npm i @boundaryml/baml@0.225.0 tsx && npx baml-cli generate --from baml_src", "command": "node server.js & npx tsx test.ts", "expectation": {"check": "requires_inspection", "instructions": "The call must succeed and print `synthetic summary text`. It currently fails with `Failed to parse into a response accepted by ...ChatCompletionGeneric<...>` caused by ``duplicate field `output_tokens_details` ``. Control: removing the `output_tokens_details` entry from response.json makes the same call succeed, confirming the failure is the usage-field alias collision and not the completion content."}}, {"files": {"test.ts": "import { b } from ''./baml_client''\nb.Extract(''hi'').then(console.log, (e) => console.error(String(e)))\n", "server.js": "const fs = require(''fs'')\nrequire(''http'').createServer((req, res) => res.end(fs.readFileSync(''response.json''))).listen(8787)\n", "response.json": "{\n  \"id\": \"chatcmpl-example\",\n  \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n  \"created\": 1787007845,\n  \"model\": \"accounts/fireworks/models/deepseek-v4-flash-0731\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    {\n      \"index\": 0,\n      \"message\": { \"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"synthetic summary text\", \"tools\": null },\n      \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"prompt_tokens\": 100,\n    \"completion_tokens\": 20,\n    \"total_tokens\": 120,\n    \"prompt_tokens_details\": { \"cached_tokens\": 99 },\n    \"input_tokens_details\": { \"cached_tokens\": 99 }\n  }\n}\n", "baml_src/main.baml": "generator ts {\n    output_type \"typescript\"\n    output_dir \"../\"\n    version \"0.225.0\"\n    default_client_mode async\n}\n\nclient<llm> Mock {\n    provider \"openai-generic\"\n    options {\n        base_url \"http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1\"\n        api_key \"x\"\n        model \"x\"\n    }\n}\n\nfunction Extract(text: string) -> string {\n    client Mock\n    prompt #\"{{ text }}\"#\n}\n"}, "setup": "npm i @boundaryml/baml@0.225.0 tsx && npx baml-cli generate --from baml_src", "command": "node server.js & npx tsx test.ts", "expectation": {"check": "requires_inspection", "instructions": "Same defect on the input/prompt pair. The call must succeed and print `synthetic summary text`; it currently fails with ``duplicate field `input_tokens_details` ``. This repro ensures the fix covers both alias pairs, not just the output/completion one."}}, {"files": {"test.ts": "import { b } from ''./baml_client''\nb.Extract(''hi'').then(console.log, (e) => console.error(String(e)))\n", "server.js": "const fs = require(''fs'')\nrequire(''http'').createServer((req, res) => res.end(fs.readFileSync(''response.json''))).listen(8787)\n", "response.json": "{\n  \"id\": \"chatcmpl-example\",\n  \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n  \"created\": 1787007845,\n  \"model\": \"accounts/fireworks/models/deepseek-v4-flash-0731\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    {\n      \"index\": 0,\n      \"message\": { \"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"synthetic summary text\", \"tools\": null },\n      \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"prompt_tokens\": 100,\n    \"completion_tokens\": 20,\n    \"total_tokens\": 120,\n    \"prompt_tokens_details\": { \"cached_tokens\": 99 },\n    \"completion_tokens_details\": { \"reasoning_tokens\": 0 },\n    \"output_tokens_details\": { \"reasoning_tokens\": 0 }\n  }\n}\n", "baml_src/main.baml": "generator ts {\n    output_type \"typescript\"\n    output_dir \"../\"\n    version \"0.225.0\"\n    default_client_mode async\n}\n\nclient<llm> Mock {\n    provider \"openai\"\n    options {\n        base_url \"http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1\"\n        api_key \"x\"\n        model \"x\"\n    }\n}\n\nfunction Extract(text: string) -> string {\n    client Mock\n    prompt #\"{{ text }}\"#\n}\n"}, "setup": "npm i @boundaryml/baml@0.225.0 tsx && npx baml-cli generate --from baml_src", "command": "node server.js & npx tsx test.ts", "expectation": {"check": "requires_inspection", "instructions": "Identical failure via the dedicated `openai` provider, which shares the same deserializer. The call must succeed and print `synthetic summary text`. The reporter observed the same failure on the streaming path (`b.stream`), where usage arrives in the final SSE chunk — verify the fix there as well."}}], "closed_on_github": true}'::jsonb, 'eval'),
('fixed:gh-4587', 'fixed', '{"id": "gh-4587", "number": 4587, "title": "0.17.0: `throws` clause with an unresolved type panics the compiler (index out of bounds, type_ref.rs:346, exit 134) — 0.16.0 gives a clean E0002", "repros": [{"files": {"baml_src/main.baml": "client C = openai.GenericClient.new(model = \"m\", base_url = env.BASE_URL, api_key = env.API_KEY);\n\nfunction Hello(name: string) -> string throws ai.errors.LlmClient {\n    client: C\n    prompt: `${role(\"user\")}Say hello to ${name}.`\n}\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "baml check --from .", "expectation": {"check": "should_not_compile", "diagnostic_contains": "E0002"}}, {"files": {"baml_src/main.baml": "client C = openai.GenericClient.new(model = \"m\", base_url = env.BASE_URL, api_key = env.API_KEY);\n\nfunction Hello(name: string) -> string throws baml.errors.LlmClient {\n    client: C\n    prompt: `${role(\"user\")}Say hello to ${name}.`\n}\n"}, "setup": null, "command": "baml check --from .", "expectation": {"check": "should_compile"}}], "closed_on_github": true}'::jsonb, 'eval');
